    "content": "Mogadishu — Somali Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre has announced changes to the heads of several government departments, a move officials say is intended to accelerate the implementation of ongoing projects and improve administrative efficiency. The reshuffle, which was announced on Thursday, affects director general positions in at least three ministries.\n\nIn a statement, the Prime Minister's office said the appointments were made under Article 119(D) of the Federal Republic of Somalia's constitution. Dr. Mohamed Saneey Dalmar has been named Director General of the Ministry of Ports and Marine Transport, while Ahmed Yusuf Abdulle has been appointed to lead the Ministry of Energy and Water Resources. Abdullahi Hassan Adan has also received a new assignment as Director General of a ministry, though the specific portfolio was not clarified in the announcement.\n\nThe changes come as the federal government seeks to address delays in service delivery and infrastructure projects, which have been a concern for citizens and international partners. The reshuffle is seen as part of a broader effort to strengthen institutional capacity and ensure that key ministries are led by experienced administrators.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, who often follow developments in the homeland closely, such administrative changes signal a push for improved governance. Transparency in appointments and effective management of ministries are particularly important for diaspora members considering investments in sectors like energy, ports, and water resources. Reliable leadership in these areas can help create a more favorable environment for business and economic growth.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/08/06/raiisul-wasaare-xamsa-oo-isbedel-ku-sameeyay-saddex-agaasime-guud/",
